{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-514", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/514", "wordCount": 1255, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "Hello. I'm Jonathan Davis,"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "web technologies evangelist for"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "the Safari and WebKit teams."}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "Welcome to Auditing Web Content"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "with Web Inspector."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "In the process of building web"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "content, developers have a lot"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "of details to check."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "Maybe it's following a CSS class"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "name convention or ensuring good"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "accessibility on the page."}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "There can be so many details"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "that they're easy to forget and"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "tedious to find the issues."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "A built-in checklist would be"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "ideal."}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "Some teams set up automated"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "testing in a continuous"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "integration system using"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "technologies like Safari's"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "WebDriver, available for macOS"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "and now iOS."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "WebDriver is a great tool for"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "catching code changes that break"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "expected functionality for"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "users."}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "But for web developers who want"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "to check that their in-progress"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "work meets code expectations,"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "Web Inspector now includes a new"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "audit system available with"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "Safari 13 on macOS that provides"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "a quick, easy and more"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "convenient way to check web"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "In this video, I'll show you how"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "to use audits in Web Inspector,"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "how to work with tests and"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "understand their results, and"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "finally I'll cover how to create"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "custom audits for your projects."}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "To get started, you'll need to"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "enable the Develop menu to"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "access Web Inspector."}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "Just load up Safari Preferences,"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "click on Advanced and click to"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "enable the Show Develop Menu in"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "Menu Bar option."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "Now just load up a web page and"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "open Web Inspector from the"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "Develop menu."}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "Or use the keyboard shortcut"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "Command-Option-I."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "Let's take a look at WebKit.org"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "as an example."}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "Click over to the audit tab."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "And in the left sidebar is a"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "list of audits."}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "Click the arrow to the left of"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "an audit to expand it."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "An audit is a collection of test"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "groups and tests."}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "Test groups don't have any"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "functionality except to act as"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "organizational containers for a"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "collection of individual tests."}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "It's easy to run audits."}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "Click the Start button to run"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "all of the available audits."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "Or you can right click on an"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "audit for a contextual menu with"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "more actions."}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "To run a single audit, right"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "click on the audit and select"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "Start."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "Or you can hover over the right"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "area of the side bar and a play"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "button will appear."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "Or click to select it and press"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "the space bar."}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "Audits are fast and update in"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "real time as tests are"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "completed."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "Another way to control which"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "audits are run is to click the"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "Edit button at the bottom of the"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "navigation sidebar."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Here you can toggle the"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "checkboxes on the row next to"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "individual tests, test groups or"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "entire audits to selectively"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "enable or disable them."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "Click the done button at the"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "bottom when you're finished"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "editing."}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "A list of any collected results"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "will appear below the audits in"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "a results folder with each of"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "the results collected into Run"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "folders."}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "Expand the Run folder to access"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "the results of the audit for"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "that run."}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "The result runs are kept"}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "available across reloads of the"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "page so you can modify the"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "webpage and rerun the audit for"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "updated results."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "That way you can compare the"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "pass rate for example."}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "Results will be cleared when Web"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "Inspector is closed."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "Clicking on the results of the"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "demo audit run displays a report"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "that shows example result levels"}, {"start": 215.0, "text": "and result data."}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "The first three result levels"}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "should be familiar if you've"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "ever used XCode."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "The passed level shows a test"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "that's passed, meaning the code"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "met the expectations of the"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "test."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "Warning is a soft pass."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "It says even though the code"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "passed the test, there are"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "things that could be changed."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "Failed tells you the code did"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "not pass the test."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "The other two result levels are"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "special to audits in Web"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "Inspector."}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "An error result occurs when the"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "JavaScript being run for the"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "test throws an error."}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "Unsupported is a special case"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "that can be used to indicate"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "when the data being tested isn't"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "supported by the current page,"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "such as when there's some"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "missing API."}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "Test results can also include"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "data from the test in the form"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "of DOM nodes or error messages."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "Web Inspector includes some"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "built-in audits by default which"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "can be disabled but not deleted."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "One of the default audits"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "provides tests that check a"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "webpage for mark-up that meets"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "some common guidelines for good"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "accessibility."}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "Let's dig into the results of"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "running the accessibility audit"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "on WebKit.org."}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "The overall score shows that"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "WebKit does fairly well."}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "But there's room for"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "improvement."}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "In the failure cases shown in"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "the results, the DOM node where"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "the failure was detected is"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "shown as an interactive DOM"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "tree."}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "Expanding the DOM tree for the"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "node allows you to access child"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "nodes."}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "And hovering over them will"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "highlight the specific elements"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "on the page, just like using the"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "elements tab."}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "This makes it trivially easy to"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "understand what code in your web"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "content needs improvement."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "To fix this, I can simply click"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "this arrow to go right to the"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "node in the elements tab."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "The problem is elements with the"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "role of menu need their child"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "elements to have a role of menu"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "item."}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "So I simply need to add a new"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "role attribute with a value of"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "menu item to each of the child"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "elements of the menu."}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "I'm going to quickly add the"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "missing attribute to each of"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "these elements."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "Just a couple more."}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "Okay."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "Now I'll switch back to the"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "audit tab so I can rerun the"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "audit and see the new results"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "with these changes in the DOM."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "Perfect."}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "The page now passes all of the"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "tests."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "I simply need to incorporate"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "those changes into the actual"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "code for the site."}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "You can see how easy it is to"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "spot problems and fix them all"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "conveniently within Web"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "Inspector."}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "Audits and audit results can be"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "exported and re-imported."}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "Click the Export button to save"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "the results into a JSON file."}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "They can be re-imported into Web"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "Inspector with complete access"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "to the results, including"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "interactive DOM nodes, when"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "elements on the page match the"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "nodes in the report."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "You can also export the built-in"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "audits to see an example of how"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "to write your own audits."}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "As most teams will have their"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "own unique code objectives,"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "writing your own custom audits"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "is one of the most powerful"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "aspects of using the audit"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "framework in Web Inspector."}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "They use a JSON format to make"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "them portable."}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "Each test is simply a"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "stringified JavaScript function"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "giving you a simple framework"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "with special access to more data"}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "than you can normally access in"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "JavaScript."}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "Being simple JSON, it's easy to"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "share your tests with your team"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "or other developers."}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "There's an example ESLint audit"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "available on the WebKit blog"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "post about creating Web"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "Inspector audits."}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "The blog post goes into detail"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "about how to write a custom"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "audit as well as other powerful"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "capabilities of using the audit"}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "framework."}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "Simply download the ESLint JSON"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "file and you can easily drag and"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "drop the file onto Web Inspector"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "to import it."}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "Audits in Web Inspector are"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "quick and convenient, so I hope"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "you'll give them a try using the"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "built-in accessibility audit on"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "your own web pages."}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "Use the portable audit format to"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "create your own audits and"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "ensure in-progress code meets"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "your project standards."}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "And we love hearing from you and"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "hope you'll file bug reports for"}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "any issues you find or feature"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "requests you might have."}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "For more information and"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "additional resources about what"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "I've covered, use the links in"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "the resources section associated"}]}
